                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2e9cf5ba-5222-31f6-9cf0-a2961bbb78b4",
                                        "entry_id": "3e6a6316-6214-397b-9c54-c10f814dedf0",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A system of ethics based on the premise that something's value may be measured by its usefulness."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "52f33ac4-0f23-3435-8912-a42e427ef8e8",
                                        "entry_id": "3e6a6316-6214-397b-9c54-c10f814dedf0",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The theory that action should be directed toward achieving the \\\"greatest happiness for the greatest number of people\\\" (hedonistic universalism), or one of various related theories."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "77c186f3-7b0c-3f33-8db0-366f28200e45",
                                        "entry_id": "3e6a6316-6214-397b-9c54-c10f814dedf0",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Practicality, functionality, as opposed to e.g. aesthetics."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8675927d-43f6-438c-bcd9-a64bee14d2f1",
                                                "sense_id": "77c186f3-7b0c-3f33-8db0-366f28200e45",
                                                "text": "After a few more concerts, my uneasiness took form: the response seemed only to be to the Interpreter as Performer. The reviews praised her artistry. But I heard few women speak of her as a bridge in communication for deaf women, about her function, her \"utilitarianism.\""
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "d20e4bec-1139-4cbe-8975-061c84cfb61d",
                        "source_entry_id": "3ab9ed51-dbb7-360c-86f4-81e0f21587cc",
                        "source_sense_id": "49366800-d9ea-3a3b-a83d-a6b416173b8d",
                        "target_lang_word": "utilitarisme",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "utilitarisme",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "128ceac3-b7e0-3258-9024-733c4837645f",
                                        "entry_id": "555f2bad-b0df-32e7-a2a8-3d5f244bfae8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Doctrine qui consiste à ramener la notion du bien à celle de l’utilité, à faire de l’intérêt le principe du droit et de la morale."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "fbaad07a-6fb8-3a92-823d-109fd4dfc0ee",
                                        "entry_id": "555f2bad-b0df-32e7-a2a8-3d5f244bfae8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "(Plus récemment, notamment chez les antispécistes) Doctrine qui mesure la moralité d’une action à l’aune des conséquences, positives ou négatives, qu’elle produit chez tous les êtres sensibles — humains et animaux — concernés."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "especially"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "39161df9-9da5-3df5-95ea-927279bcc3f0",
                                        "entry_id": "555f2bad-b0df-32e7-a2a8-3d5f244bfae8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Action politique inspirée par l’utilitarisme."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "broadly"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3f06dff4-dd99-4ea6-a514-baa49f67771c",
                                                "sense_id": "39161df9-9da5-3df5-95ea-927279bcc3f0",
                                                "text": "Alors que la réponse attendue devrait être, au minimum minimorum, de réhabiliter les grands auteurs, le pouvoir enchaîne des décisions allégeant les exigences en lettres et en langues, pour les élèves comme pour les enseignants, au nom d’un utilitarisme ringardisant le passé."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
